 This code demonstrates inheritance by using the Libro class as a base class and the Encyclopedia class as a derived class. The Libro class contains attributes (title, author, publisher, and publication_date) and a method  (print_info()) that displays libro information. The Encyclopedia class inherits from Libro through class Encyclopedia(Libro ), allowing it to reuse the base class attributes and methods. It adds its own attributes; edition and num_pages, and overrides the print_info() method to include encyclopedia-specific information. The code accesses methods and attributes from the base class by calling Libro._ init_(self, ...) to initialize inherited attributes   and Libro.print_info(self) to display the base class information before printing the new attributes.
 


